Package: plotgif
Title: Stitch a List of R Plots into an Animated GIF
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Grey", "Monroe", email = "gmonroe@ucdavis.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Give make_gif() a list of plots (ggplot objects, or functions that draw with
    base graphics) and it writes one PNG frame per plot and stitches them into a GIF with the
    file name, pixel dimensions, frame rate, and output directory you choose. One function;
    the frames are whatever you can draw. Built for PLS 206 (UC Davis) course materials.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
